  273: the selected clean guest reaches the GUI, persists, positively identifies its
  274: translator, and supplies complete negative Rosetta evidence. Budget at least
  275: one provision/fix/clean-rerun cycle before declaring failure final.
  276: 
  277: ## 10. Phase 4 - sequential integration with the real M1-M6 launcher
  278: 
  279: This phase starts only after the Phase 3 package/profile is reviewed. It must
  280: not edit launcher files in the M7 development worktree.
  281: 
  282: 1. Create a fresh worktree and integration branch at the immutable Phase 0
  283:    commit resolved from `luna/macos-m6-followups`. Record `git status`, commit,
  284:    and the mapping from reviewed M7 commits/files into this candidate.
  285: 2. Merge/cherry-pick the reviewed M7 build/package/profile units, resolve them
  286:    against the real M1-M6 layout, then implement launcher selection only in
  287:    this worktree. Shared launcher files including `main.go`, `detect.go`, macOS
  288:    lifecycle/Lima/profile files, and their tests belong exclusively here.
  289: 3. Expose `--profile auto|rosetta-amd64|native-arm64`. Explicit CLI wins,
  290:    persisted owner choice is next, otherwise `auto`. Until promotion, `auto`
  291:    continues to default to Rosetta; the test hook for native preference must be
  292:    explicit. Native preflight is non-mutating and checks Apple Silicon,
  293:    Lima/VZ, digests, translator, and resources. Forced native fails closed.
  294: 4. In the combined candidate on the physical Mac, run and retain raw evidence
  295:    for: forced native success; forced native preflight/runtime failure; forced
  296:    Rosetta success and canary; auto native selection under the explicit test
  297:    policy; auto fallback from failed native to actual Rosetta; persisted choice;
  298:    separate VM/state paths and host sync; recovery after half-created native VM;
  299:    and recovery after forced launcher/VM termination. Unit tests or two
  300:    unrelated installed launchers cannot close these cases.
  301: 5. `status`/`diagnose` reports requested/selected profile, fallback reason,
  302:    backend/vm type, guest/kernel and supervisor/IOL architecture, translator
  303:    name/version, and `rosetta_present`. Preserve M1-M6 loopback exposure,
  304:    readiness semantics, i386 truthfulness, and Windows builds/tests.
  305: 6. After any integration defect, apply the smallest fix and rerun the failed
  306:    case plus forced-native, forced-Rosetta, auto-fallback, isolation, and
  307:    recovery. Budget at least one complete defect/fix/rerun cycle.
  308: 
  309: **Blocked by:** reviewed Phase 3 units, frozen M1-M6 source/artifact, and the
  310: identified physical Mac.
  311: 
  312: **Exit:** one combined artifact passes forced native, forced Rosetta, automatic
  313: selection/fallback, state isolation, status truthfulness, and recovery. This
  314: phase is mandatory before Phase 7 can choose PROMOTE.
  315: 
  316: ## 11. Phase 5 - rerun the authoritative M3/M4 hardware matrix
  317: 
  318: Run the combined Phase 4 candidate on the physical Mac using the exact Phase 0
  319: procedures, browser steps, labs, image hash, expected observations, and result
  320: formats. Do not replace browser operations with API calls. A row may use a
  321: replacement only when its Phase 0 owner-approved equivalence mapping exists.
  322: 
  323: | Matrix group | Required observation |
  324: |---|---|
  325: | Browser lifecycle | Safari or Chrome performs upload, registration, lab creation/start, console input, stop, reload, and saved-lab recovery |
  326: | Host data/sync | Images/labs under `~/Library/Application Support/iolbox` survive launcher and VM restart; spaces and non-ASCII paths round-trip |
  327: | Consoles/forwarding | Two simultaneous browser consoles work; GUI, console, and capture are Mac-loopback-only |
  328: | Capture | Live traffic appears; multi-link and soak captures produce non-empty valid pcapng opened by Wireshark or saved by browser |
  329: | VPCS/IOL | Native-arm64 VPCS and translated x86_64 IOL exchange bidirectional traffic with counts/loss/latency; this also closes the substitute VPCS suite when upstream has none |
  330: | Multi-link | Every expected path forwards and teardown is clean |
  331: | NAT | Outbound connectivity works in the qualified mode and stop removes NAT state |
  332: | Extnet | Attach, traffic, detach, and cleanup pass on the frozen interface/mapping |
  333: | Capacity | Authoritative two-node and four-IOL-node labs reach prompts and forward traffic on the approved tier |
  334: | Traffic soak | Continuous traffic runs two hours with capture active; record loss, faults, exits, CPU/load, and memory throughout |
  335: | Forced termination | Separate launcher and VM terminations recover without stale taps, bridges, processes, sockets, or corrupt state |
  336: | Rosetta exclusion | Complete mount/binfmt/process inventory before, during IOL execution, and after restart is Rosetta-free |
  337: 
  338: A defect gets the smallest owning fix and reruns the row plus adjacent
  339: teardown/restart rows. The four-node/traffic-soak schedule includes at least one
  340: defect/fix/full-soak rerun cycle.
  341: 
  342: **Blocked by:** any mandatory Phase 0 input/mapping, physical Mac, owner
  343: image/licence, Phase 4 candidate, browser access, or approved hardware tier.
  344: 
  345: **Exit:** every row is PASS. An unavailable extnet or authoritative fixture is
  346: BLOCKED and prevents promotion; it is never rounded up to a complete matrix.
  347: 
  348: ## 12. Phase 6 - same-machine Rosetta versus native A/B metrics
  349: 
  350: On the same physical Mac, rerun the exact shipped Rosetta artifact and combined
  351: native candidate with identical macOS/Lima, vCPU/RAM, image hash, labs, capture,
  352: and cache conditions. For two-node and four-node cases collect at least three
  353: runs, retaining every raw value, median, and worst case:
  354: 
  355: - cold VM start to successful `GET /` and lab start to all usable prompts;
  356: - traffic counts, loss, and latency;
  357: - host CPU, guest load, and translator CPU at idle/during traffic;
  358: - per-IOL/VPCS/supervisor RSS, guest used/peak memory and swap;
  359: - Mac memory pressure and used/peak memory;
  360: - teardown duration and stale-resource count;
  361: - translator crashes, SIGILL/SIGSYS, and unexpected exits.
  362: 
  363: Default thresholds, subject to owner approval before collection:
  364: 
  365: - any new functional failure, crash, SIGILL/SIGSYS, stale resource, or Rosetta
  366:   dependency is unacceptable;
  367: - median VM or lab boot more than 25% slower than baseline is unacceptable;
  368: - median steady-state CPU, guest/host memory, or aggregate node RSS more than
  369:   25% worse is unacceptable;
  370: - worse Mac memory-pressure state, sustained swap, or inability to run the
  371:   approved four-node tier is unacceptable;
  372: - packet loss more than one percentage point worse, failure of the functional
  373:   ping target, or any traffic-soak interruption is unacceptable.
  374: 
  375: Thresholds may not be relaxed after results are seen without recording a new
  376: decision and repeating the promotion review. Every completed run/result to
  377: which an approved threshold applies receives PASS or FAIL immediately. Any
  378: completed run exceeding its approved threshold is FAIL and forces
  379: NO-PROMOTE; it cannot be reclassified as HOLD or ƒ?oinsufficient sample.ƒ?? A
  380: missing metric is UNEVALUATED, never zero.
  381: 
  382: **Blocked by:** both exact artifacts, stable same-Mac conditions, labs/image,
  383: and approved thresholds.
  384: 
  385: **Exit:** raw runs, summaries, deltas, and threshold verdicts exist for every
  386: metric/topology. Include one defect/fix/rerun cycle if the first collection is
  387: invalid due to a product or measurement defect; a genuine threshold failure
  388: remains failure.
  389: 
  390: ## 13. Phase 7 - mechanical promotion decision
  391: 
  392: The gate ledger contains one row per atomic acceptance gate, with exactly one
  393: canonical raw evidence item and one verdict in that row. The categories below
  394: expand into separate rows (for example, each live gate, matrix row, and A/B
  395: threshold is its own gate); they must not be collapsed into one summary row:
  396: 
  397: 1. native substrate provenance/attestation;
  398: 2. supervisor tests, truthful hello, VPCS upstream-or-substitute suite, rootfs,
  399:    and all five Phase 1 live gates;
  400: 3. selected translator correctness JSON and Phase 3 measured bake-off;
  401: 4. selected physical-Mac guest translator-positive/Rosetta-negative inventory;
  402: 5. combined M1-M6+M7 launcher forced-native, forced-Rosetta, auto-fallback,
  403:    isolation, and recovery results;
  404: 6. every authoritative M3/M4 matrix row;
  405: 7. every two-/four-node A/B threshold;
  406: 8. legal hygiene and translator notices/obligations.
  407: 
  408: Outcomes are mechanical and mutually exclusive:
  409: 
  410: - **PROMOTE:** every gate is PASS. No FAIL, UNEVALUATED, or BLOCKED gate may
  411:   coexist with PROMOTE. Enable native eligibility for `auto` only in this
  412:   reviewed combined line and retain explicit Rosetta fallback. **A mechanical
  413:   PROMOTE verdict is not self-executing.** Per owner ruling recorded in
  414:   `docs/m7-evidence/phase0/threshold-approval.md`, it authorizes the gate
  415:   ledger's own PROMOTE label only; merging this line, tagging a release, or
  416:   publishing an artifact requires a separate, explicit owner sign-off after
  417:   the owner has personally reviewed the actual measured results. No
  418:   implementation or review session may treat PROMOTE as authorization to
  419:   merge or ship.
  420: - **NO-PROMOTE:** any evaluated gate is FAIL, including any completed run that
  421:   exceeds an approved threshold. Later inconvenience, sample concerns, or a
  422:   packaging label cannot downgrade a failure.
  423: - **HOLD / EXPERIMENTAL:** no gate has failed, but a predeclared packaging issue
  424:   or genuinely inconclusive/missing evidence leaves at least one gate
  425:   UNEVALUATED. HOLD cannot override FAIL and keeps `auto` on Rosetta.
  426: - **BLOCKED:** no gate has failed, but an absent external dependency listed in
  427:   section 4 prevents evaluation and at least one gate is BLOCKED. Ordinary code
  428:   defects and measured regressions are not BLOCKED. BLOCKED cannot coexist
  429:   with PROMOTE.
  430: 
  431: `docs/macos-m7-result.md` must reproduce the ledger and outcome. Each row links
  432: one raw item and states one verdict; no gate may cite only a prose summary.
  433: `docs/macos-m7-handoff.md` lists remaining work without implying unrun checks
  434: passed.
  435: 
  436: ## 14. Engineering-time and wait model
  437: 
  438: Ranges are focused engineering days for one competent implementer. Likely and
  439: worst ranges explicitly include at least one investigate/fix/rerun cycle in
  440: translator qualification, guest provisioning, launcher integration, and the
  441: four-node/traffic-soak work. They exclude owner and hardware queue time.
  442: 
  443: | Phase | Best | Likely | Worst | Included contingency |
  444: |---|---:|---:|---:|---|
  445: | 0 - contracts/inputs | 0.5 | 1 | 2 | One evidence-contract correction |
  446: | 1 - native builds/live gates | 1.5 | 3 | 5 | Architecture-validation or live-gate fix/rerun |
  447: | 2 - translator rehearsal | 1 | 2.5 | 5 | One translator fault investigation/fix/full rerun |
  448: | 3 - guest provisioning/bake-off | 2 | 4 | 7 | One provisioning defect/fix/three-clean-run repeat |
  449: | 4 - real launcher integration | 2 | 4 | 7 | Merge defect plus full selection/fallback/isolation/recovery rerun |
  450: | 5 - M3/M4 matrix | 2 | 4 | 7 | Four-node or soak defect/fix and full two-hour rerun |
  451: | 6 - same-Mac A/B | 1.5 | 3 | 5 | One invalid measurement/product-fix dataset rerun |
  452: | 7 - decision/handoff | 0.5 | 1 | 2 | Ledger/review correction |
  453: | **Total engineering** | **11** | **22.5** | **40** | Excludes external waits |
  454: 
  455: External wait time is reported separately per phase: owner approval and source
  456: artifact delivery (Phases 0/4-7), native-arm64 target allocation or hosted-runner
  457: documentation (Phases 1-2), FEX installation approval (Phase 2), physical Mac
  458: scheduling (Phases 3-7), browser/extnet access (Phase 5), and uninterrupted
  459: two-hour plus rerun windows (Phases 5-6). Wait time is calendar time and may
  460: exceed engineering time; it is never hidden inside a focused-day estimate.
  461: 
  462: The master plan's 3-5 focused-day M7 estimate is a historical happy-path number,
  463: not a commitment for this expanded evidence program. Every earlier Mac phase
  464: encountered hardware defects beyond its estimate; schedule and report this work
  465: from the ranges above.
  466: 
  467: ## 15. Implementation order and stop conditions
  468: 
  469: 1. Freeze Phase 0 contracts, authoritative inputs, targets, thresholds, and
  470:    immutable M1-M6 source commit.
  471: 2. Run Phase 1 native builds, VPCS tests, fail-closed validation, and five live
  472:    gates. Missing native substrate/capabilities is BLOCKED.
  473: 3. Run Phase 2 correctness rehearsal. No eligible translator is NO-PROMOTE.
  474: 4. Run Phase 3 clean provisioning and measured bake-off on the physical Mac.
  475: 5. Sequentially create the fresh M1-M6 worktree and complete Phase 4 combined
  476:    launcher integration. Do not run promotion gates against unrelated binaries.
  477: 6. Run Phases 5-6 authoritative matrix and A/B evidence on that combined
  478:    candidate.
  479: 7. Apply Phase 7 rules and write result/handoff documents. PROMOTE is impossible
  480:    until every prior gate is PASS.
  481: 
  482: During implementation, stage exact paths only; never use `git add .` or
  483: `git add -A`. Unrelated dirty or untracked files belong to the owner.
