  233: ## Two real harness bugs found and fixed this session (mine, not sol's ƒ?" small and directly in scope)
  234: 
  235: After confirming native-arm64 boots cleanly, its first two ping runs showed
  236: **0% or unparseable connectivity** despite both consoles reaching real
  237: prompts. Root-caused, not guessed:
  238: 
  239: 1. **VPCS never got its IP configured.** `macos_m4_runtime_darwin_test.go`
  240:    itself documents: *"vpcs is the one node kind with no boot-time config
  241:    path in the supervisor"* ƒ?" the M4 reference test always types
  242:    `config.commands` via console itself; nothing auto-applies them. My
  243:    harness sent the ping immediately without this step. Fixed by sending
  244:    `ip 192.168.1.10 192.168.1.1 24` to PC1's console before the first ping,
  245:    matching the reference implementation's own documented requirement.
  246: 2. **This VPCS build never prints an aggregate ping summary line** (no
  247:    "X packets transmitted..." trailer at all ƒ?" confirmed via raw console
  248:    capture), matching another comment in the same reference test file.
  249:    Added a fallback parser counting individual `bytes from ... icmp_seq=N`
  250:    reply lines and `icmp_seq=N timeout` lines directly (same approach the
  251:    reference test's own `m4VPCSReplyRE`/`m4VPCSTimeoutRE` use).
  252: 
  253: Both fixes verified live: subsequent native-arm64 runs show real,
  254: consistent ping data (see table below). `python3 -m py_compile` clean
  255: before each deploy.
