  316: ## 11. Phase 5 - rerun the authoritative M3/M4 hardware matrix
  317: 
  318: Run the combined Phase 4 candidate on the physical Mac using the exact Phase 0
  319: procedures, browser steps, labs, image hash, expected observations, and result
  320: formats. Do not replace browser operations with API calls. A row may use a
  321: replacement only when its Phase 0 owner-approved equivalence mapping exists.
  322: 
  323: | Matrix group | Required observation |
  324: |---|---|
  325: | Browser lifecycle | Safari or Chrome performs upload, registration, lab creation/start, console input, stop, reload, and saved-lab recovery |
  326: | Host data/sync | Images/labs under `~/Library/Application Support/iolbox` survive launcher and VM restart; spaces and non-ASCII paths round-trip |
  327: | Consoles/forwarding | Two simultaneous browser consoles work; GUI, console, and capture are Mac-loopback-only |
  328: | Capture | Live traffic appears; multi-link and soak captures produce non-empty valid pcapng opened by Wireshark or saved by browser |
  329: | VPCS/IOL | Native-arm64 VPCS and translated x86_64 IOL exchange bidirectional traffic with counts/loss/latency; this also closes the substitute VPCS suite when upstream has none |
  330: | Multi-link | Every expected path forwards and teardown is clean |
  331: | NAT | Outbound connectivity works in the qualified mode and stop removes NAT state |
  332: | Extnet | Attach, traffic, detach, and cleanup pass on the frozen interface/mapping |
  333: | Capacity | Authoritative two-node and four-IOL-node labs reach prompts and forward traffic on the approved tier |
  334: | Traffic soak | Continuous traffic runs two hours with capture active; record loss, faults, exits, CPU/load, and memory throughout |
  335: | Forced termination | Separate launcher and VM terminations recover without stale taps, bridges, processes, sockets, or corrupt state |
  336: | Rosetta exclusion | Complete mount/binfmt/process inventory before, during IOL execution, and after restart is Rosetta-free |
  337: 
  338: A defect gets the smallest owning fix and reruns the row plus adjacent
  339: teardown/restart rows. The four-node/traffic-soak schedule includes at least one
