    1: # Phase 6 regression-threshold approval
    2: 
    3: Status: **APPROVED**
    4: 
    5: The owner approved the thresholds below, exactly as proposed by section 12 of
    6: `docs/macos-m7-plan.md`, in this session (2026-08-17). They are now frozen and
    7: apply to Phase 6 threshold A/B collection.
    8: 
    9: ## Proposed thresholds
   10: 
   11: For identical same-Mac Rosetta/native two-node and four-node runs:
   12: 
   13: 1. Any new functional failure, crash, `SIGILL`, `SIGSYS`, stale resource, or
   14:    Rosetta dependency is unacceptable.
   15: 2. A median VM boot or lab boot more than 25% slower than the shipped
   16:    baseline is unacceptable.
   17: 3. Median steady-state CPU, guest/host memory, or aggregate node RSS more
   18:    than 25% worse than baseline is unacceptable.
   19: 4. A worse Mac memory-pressure state, sustained swap, or inability to run the
   20:    approved four-node tier is unacceptable.
   21: 5. Packet loss more than one percentage point worse than baseline, failure of
   22:    the functional ping target, or any traffic-soak interruption is
   23:    unacceptable.
   24: 
   25: ## Decision rules to freeze with approval
   26: 
   27: - Collect at least three runs for each two-node and four-node topology and
   28:   retain every raw value, median, and worst case.
   29: - Freeze the replacement/threshold decision before seeing candidate results;
   30:   do not relax a threshold after results are known without recording a new
   31:   decision and repeating the promotion review.
   32: - Every completed run/result to which an approved threshold applies receives
   33:   `PASS` or `FAIL` immediately.
   34: - Any completed run exceeding an approved threshold is `FAIL` and forces
   35:   `NO-PROMOTE`; it cannot be reclassified as `HOLD` or ƒ?oinsufficient sample.ƒ??
