   33: ## 1. How verdicts were assigned
   34: 
   35: Four values only, per the frozen contract: `PASS`, `FAIL`, `UNEVALUATED`,
   36: `BLOCKED`.
   37: 
   38: The scoring rules actually applied, all quoted from the frozen documents:
   39: 
   40: 1. **"No gate may cite only a prose summary."** (plan A13) A row whose only
   41:    support is a handoff's or `STATUS.md`'s narrative claim is `UNEVALUATED`,
   42:    however confident that narrative is. This single rule is responsible for
   43:    most `UNEVALUATED` rows below.
   44: 2. **"A summary or alternate copy cannot replace the named raw file."**
   45:    (gate-ledger preamble) Evidence that exists only on the physical Mac and
   46:    was never copied into the repository cannot close a row.
   47: 3. **"A missing metric is `UNEVALUATED`, never zero."**
   48:    (`phase0/threshold-approval.md`, plan A12)
   49: 4. **"Every completed run/result to which an approved threshold applies
   50:    receives `PASS` or `FAIL` immediately. Any completed run exceeding an
   51:    approved threshold is `FAIL` and forces `NO-PROMOTE`; it cannot be
   52:    reclassified as `HOLD` or 'insufficient sample.'"**
   53:    (`phase0/threshold-approval.md`)
   54: 5. **"Later inconvenience, sample concerns, or a packaging label cannot
   55:    downgrade a failure."** (plan A13) An owner waiver is an *override*
   56:    recorded alongside the row, not a mechanical re-score of it.
   57: 
   58: ### A note on rows 1 and 2
   59: 
   60: Applying rules 1 and 2 honestly is the most consequential judgement in this
   61: document, and it cuts against work that was genuinely done. Phases 4, 5 and 7
   62: really were executed on real hardware, and their handoffs are detailed and
   63: candid. But the contract's canonical directory layouts
   64: (`phase4/<machine-id>/<run-id>/provenance/ƒ?Ý`,
   65: `phase5/<machine-id>/<run-id>/matrix/ƒ?Ý/row.log`,
   66: `phase6/<machine-id>/<run-id>/ƒ?Ý/thresholds/*.log`) **do not exist in the
   67: repository at all**, and for Phases 5 and 7 the underlying raw artifacts were
   68: left on the Mac. A ledger that scored those rows `PASS` on the strength of the
   69: handoff text would be exactly the "prose summary" closure section 13 forbids.
   70: 
   71: This is not a claim the work did not happen. It is a claim that **the
